    // The old version hooked NetSessionRPCs.RPC_KickPlayer and dropped EVERY call. That was exactly
    // backwards: RPC_KickPlayer runs on the CALLER (so it blocked YOU from kicking others), and it is
    // NOT the RPC that removes you when someone kicks YOU. A kick actually works like this:
    //   kicker (host / code-owner / dev-menu) -> Nakama API KickUserFromPrivateRoom(targetUserID)
    //     -> Nakama server removes the target from the room and sends the target a notification
    //        with code PrivateRoomKicked (10)  [or Banned (-8) for a room ban]
    //     -> the TARGET's client runs NotificationManager.HandleReceivedNotification(notification),
    //        sees code 10/-8, and disconnects itself.
